MTS patch: turn-based clock (setting mtsTurnClock, default 0 = off).

Extends server/mtsGameTime.h (time-scale.patch): with mtsTurnClock=1 the
game clock only runs while below the target in mtsClockTarget.txt (run
dir), holds exactly at it, reports "<gameSeconds> <paused>" in
mtsClockNow.txt and persists itself in mtsClockGame.txt, so a restart
resumes paused at the same game time. Hooks in server.cpp: turnStep() at
the top of each main-loop pass, a 20 ms socket-wait cap (and no zero
wait on frozen events while paused), the final persist at shutdown, and
the wall clock for housekeeping that must work while paused (login
timeout, closing dead players' sockets, SAY flood gap). Off: unchanged.
See docs/turn-clock.md.

--- a/server/mtsGameTime.h
